// One window event of kind rbi_kind with the fields rbl_ev, as gfx_event filled it in, for the ribbon rib. A combo box that has the keyboard (or is pressed on) takes the event first (rbe_cb_event), and then rbe_rest does what is left. Answers bits: 1 paint the ribbon again, 2 a command was given (rib_cmd, rib_arg and rib_name), 4 the press closed a menu or ended a combo box and is not used up, so it is owed to what is under, 8 the ribbon took the event (it is in the band, or a menu is open, or a combo box has the keyboard).
rib_event(Ribbon rib, int rbi_kind, int[] rbl_ev) {
  rbe_clear();
  int rbi_c = rbe_cb_event(rib, rbi_kind, rbl_ev);
  int rbi_b = rbi_c;
} chain (Ribbon rib, int rbi_kind, int[] rbl_ev) {
  if(rbi_c == 0) {
    rbi_b = rbe_rest(rib, rbi_kind, rbl_ev);
  }
} return int rbi_b;
